{"family": "marigold_v2", "task": "depth", "name": "Marigold V2", "plain": "Relative depth from one photo by a very large image-generation model run for a single step: accurate but slow and memory-hungry (about 2 GB of GPU memory, 9 GB of host RAM).", "summary": "Marigold V2 (Pavlovic, Wandel, Obukhov et al. 2026): affine-invariant log depth by one rectified-flow step of Qwen-Image-Edit-2509's 20 B transformer (NF4 4-bit, as the authors run it) with a rank-128 depth LoRA and a fine-tuned Qwen VAE decoder (depth/Log-stage2).", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/huawei-bayerlab/marigold-v2", "upstream_commit": "main", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "Marigold V2: Revisiting Diffusion Transformers for Monocular Depth Estimation", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08084", "date": "2026-09-09", "venue": "ACM TOG (SIGGRAPH Asia 2026)", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "bfloat16", "kernels_dtype": "bfloat16", "kernel_libs": ["nf4"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": [], "no_kernels_reason": "", "no_original_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "seed", "default": 2026, "bounds": "", "effect": "output"}, {"name": "long_side", "default": 0, "bounds": ">= 0", "effect": "output"}, {"name": "exact_mask", "default": false, "bounds": "", "effect": "output"}, {"name": "stream", "default": true, "bounds": "", "effect": "output"}], "outputs": [{"name": "depth", "extra": false}], "output_info": {"kind": "affine_invariant_log"}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE", "NOTICE"], "licence_notes": ["The converted weight file (NF4 transformer, LoRA, folded constants, 2-D VAE) is hosted by fastforks under the originals' Apache-2.0 licence; NOTICE keeps both attributions and lists the changes."], "limitations": ["20 B transformer in 4 bit: 8.4 GB of weights; by default (`stream=True`, CUDA) it runs in ~1-4 GB of device memory from 8.4 GB of page-locked host RAM (load fails with an error when less is free); `stream=False` keeps it resident (about 9-11 GB of device memory, 16 GB cards: up to ~1024 px).", "Diffusion model: the portable VAE draws its posterior noise with a CPU generator seeded with `seed`. The authors' default path draws from the device generator.", "The first-ten iBims-1 and NYUv2 comparisons use the same seeded posterior noise for both implementations. The original uses the authors' NF4 weights with BF16 autocast.", "On the 16 GB reference GPU with expandable allocator segments, the original BF16 stack fits the 518 x 770 speed input and runs out of memory at 994 x 1482.", "The enlargement to a multiple of 16 is bicubic (the original: OpenCV Lanczos); inputs with sides that are multiples of 16 are not resized.", "The output is log depth up to scale and shift (`kind = \"affine_invariant_log\"`): align in log space, not with the other families' depth outputs.", "A traced or exported module reuses the noise of its traced shape; CPU inference is possible but slow (bf16 GEMMs of a 20 B model).", "Model.compile() compiles the VAE encoder and decoder around the streamed transformer. At 994 x 1482, the compiled path took 4.80 s versus 5.09 s portable. The first compiled call took 119.2 s.", "At 480 x 640, the standalone BF16 TensorRT VAE plans took 1.16 s versus 1.18 s for paired portable inference. Estimated peak allocated device memory was 2042 versus 717 MiB. The streamed NF4 transformer ran in PyTorch for both measurements."], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: a depth or inverse-depth map. `kind` (a card field, `result.kind`) says what the numbers mean: `metric` = metres; `scale_invariant`, `affine_invariant`, `affine_invariant_log` (log depth) and `affine_invariant_inverse` are relative (unknown scale or shift, not metres). Metric models that use the focal length take `model(image, intrinsics=K)` (K `[3, 3]`, pixels of the input): `metric3d-vit-large` and `da3metric-large` need it for correct metres (`da3metric-large`: metres = output x focal / 300; without `intrinsics=` a 300 px focal length is assumed, wrong for a real camera). `unidepth-v2-vitl14`, `unik3d-vitl`, `depth-pro` and MoGe estimate the camera themselves (given `intrinsics=` replace `fx`); `zoedepth-nk` and the relative models (`da3mono-large` too) take none. Normals-only models (`kind` `none`) return `result.normals` `[B, H, W, 3]` (unit vectors, camera frame: x right, y down, z forward).", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "marigold-v2-depth", "released": "0.2.0", "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "marigold-v2-depth@1", "name": "marigold-v2-depth", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {}, "licence": {"code": "Apache-2.0", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "Apache-2.0", "weights_assumed": false, "evidence": "https://huggingface.co/huawei-bayerlab/marigold-v2/blob/main/README.md (license: apache-2.0; base model Qwen/Qwen-Image-Edit-2509)", "training_data": [{"id": "unstated", "name": "not stated by the authors"}], "training_note": "Qwen-Image-Edit-2509 (Alibaba, Apache-2.0) fine-tuned (LoRA + VAE decoder) on synthetic depth data per the Marigold V2 paper (arXiv 2609.08084); the training data terms are not checked", "commercial": "yes", "reasons": [], "notes": ["data: unstated"]}, "weights": [{"name": "marigold-v2-depth-log-stage2-nf4.safetensors", "sha256": "4b4aee27acdba6ba91582b76ed374fe91bf1bb02bea3be491e04e71a54fe9f5d", "size": 8974251334, "url": "https://huggingface.co/fastforks/marigold-v2-depth-nf4/resolve/main/marigold-v2-depth-log-stage2-nf4.safetensors", "host": "Hugging Face", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}], "input_size": "any H x W >= 1, resized or padded inside the model", "tested_max": {"size": "1988x2880", "alloc_mib": 13155, "reserved_mib": 13848}, "speed": {"standard": "994x1482", "inputs": [{"input": "480x640", "scene": "", "standard": false, "modes": {}, "oom": [], "tensorrt": {"ms": 1156.421, "peak_alloc_mb": 2042, "peak_reserved_mb": 2198, "device_mb": 1556, "engi